{"term":"swamp","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5e88196629623b7b66","definition":"An area of wet (water-saturated), spongy (soft) land, often with trees, generally a rich ecosystem for certain plants and animals but ill-suited for many agricultural purposes. (A type of wetland. Compare marsh, bog, fen.)","example":"Some small Marshes and Swamps there are, but more profitable than hurtfull.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Asian swamp eel","backswamp","Bakers Swamp","Blackswamp","Brittons Swamp","Buckley Swamp","Chinese swamp cypress","data swamp","Dismal Swamp","drain the swamp","Emu Swamp","European swamp thistle","fever-swamp","fever swamp","food swamp","Greenswamp","Moggs Swamp","palaeoswamp","paleoswamp","peatswamp","Pinnacle Swamp","Reedy Swamp","Round Swamp","Six Mile Swamp","swampable","swamp angel","swamp antechinus","swamp ape","swamp ass","swamp azalea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swamp#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b0dfa14d72d1c0ec5e","definition":"A place or situation that is foul or where progress is difficult.","example":"We two...in this swamp of iniquity...together we can bring redress to an unjust world.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["Asian swamp eel","backswamp","Bakers Swamp","Blackswamp","Brittons Swamp","Buckley Swamp","Chinese swamp cypress","data swamp","Dismal Swamp","drain the swamp","Emu Swamp","European swamp thistle","fever-swamp","fever swamp","food swamp","Greenswamp","Moggs Swamp","palaeoswamp","paleoswamp","peatswamp","Pinnacle Swamp","Reedy Swamp","Round Swamp","Six Mile Swamp","swampable","swamp angel","swamp antechinus","swamp ape","swamp ass","swamp azalea"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sour